<!--
  The same measurement as lcov.info, in the format the other half of the
  supported stack emits. scripts/coverage.py parses both, so the fixture has to
  exist in both or the cross-check only proves one parse path.

  As in samples/coverage/cobertura.xml, the root lines-valid/lines-covered pair
  is the producer's own total for the WHOLE run and is deliberately larger than
  the <line> elements listed below. Those 8,004 lines are the aggregate the
  ratchet reads; the 31 elements are the one file this change touches, which is
  the only file patch coverage needs per-line data for. Writing out the other
  7,973 lines would add nothing a reader could check by hand.

  8,000 measured lines before the change, 7,600 hit = 95.00% — the floor in
  floor.json. Four uncovered lines later: 7,600 / 8,004 = 94.95%.
-->
